From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bootm: allow uncompressed XIP outside DRAM

bootm already treats an uncompressed image whose load address equals its
payload address as XIP and deliberately performs no copy.  The subsequent
LMB reservation nevertheless rejects a NOR-mapped address because only DRAM
is present in the available-memory list.

Permit that exact no-copy case to remain outside the LMB map.  All images
which are copied or decompressed still have to reserve their destination in
available RAM.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
---
 boot/bootm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/boot/bootm.c b/boot/bootm.c
--- a/boot/bootm.c
+++ b/boot/bootm.c
@@ -709,10 +709,13 @@ static int bootm_load_os(struct bootm_headers *images, int boot_progress)
 		load = (phys_addr_t)images->os.load;
 		err = lmb_alloc_mem(LMB_MEM_ALLOC_ADDR, 0, &load,
 				    (load_end - images->os.load), LMB_NONE);
-		if (err) {
+		if (err && !no_overlap) {
 			log_err("Unable to allocate memory %#lx for loading OS\n",
 				images->os.load);
 			return 1;
+		} else if (err) {
+			log_debug("Leaving XIP OS at non-DRAM address %#lx\n",
+				  images->os.load);
 		}
 	}
 
